1
00:00:00,000 --> 00:00:02,597
Watch the wheels of a Rolls-Royce as

2
00:00:02,597 --> 00:00:03,680
it drives away.

3
00:00:03,860 --> 00:00:05,200
The wheels spin,

4
00:00:05,200 --> 00:00:07,127
but the R R logo in the

5
00:00:07,127 --> 00:00:09,724
middle stays perfectly upright,

6
00:00:09,724 --> 00:00:12,070
as if it were painted on the

7
00:00:12,070 --> 00:00:12,405
air.

8
00:00:12,585 --> 00:00:13,807
It is not magic,

9
00:00:13,807 --> 00:00:16,021
and it is not a camera trick.

10
00:00:16,201 --> 00:00:19,185
Today, ten parts of a Rolls-Royce that

11
00:00:19,185 --> 00:00:21,069
look like luxury tricks,

12
00:00:21,069 --> 00:00:24,444
and the engineering reason behind each one.

13
00:00:24,795 --> 00:00:28,515
Rolls-Royce has one simple idea behind almost

14
00:00:28,515 --> 00:00:30,251
everything it builds.

15
00:00:30,431 --> 00:00:32,201
The car should feel calm,

16
00:00:32,201 --> 00:00:33,687
quiet and effortless,

17
00:00:33,687 --> 00:00:35,882
for the person in the back seat

18
00:00:35,882 --> 00:00:37,722
as much as for the driver.

19
00:00:37,902 --> 00:00:40,817
Many of its strange parts exist to

20
00:00:40,817 --> 00:00:42,617
protect that feeling,

21
00:00:42,617 --> 00:00:44,074
by hiding effort,

22
00:00:44,074 --> 00:00:47,674
noise and small annoyances that other cars

23
00:00:47,674 --> 00:00:48,874
simply accept.

24
00:00:49,223 --> 00:00:52,141
As always, every fact here comes from

25
00:00:52,141 --> 00:00:53,324
a named source,

26
00:00:53,324 --> 00:00:56,320
Rolls-Royce and automotive references,

27
00:00:56,320 --> 00:00:58,686
all listed in the description.

28
00:00:58,866 --> 00:01:00,839
Let's start with the wheels.

29
00:01:01,189 --> 00:01:03,238
Why does the logo in the middle

30
00:01:03,238 --> 00:01:05,485
of a Rolls-Royce wheel never spin?

31
00:01:05,665 --> 00:01:07,797
Because it is not attached to the

32
00:01:07,797 --> 00:01:08,185
wheel.

33
00:01:08,365 --> 00:01:10,599
The badge sits on its own small

34
00:01:10,599 --> 00:01:12,834
bearing, so it can turn freely.

35
00:01:13,014 --> 00:01:14,241
Under the badge,

36
00:01:14,241 --> 00:01:16,541
a small weight is fixed at the

37
00:01:16,541 --> 00:01:17,078
bottom.

38
00:01:17,258 --> 00:01:18,658
As the wheel turns,

39
00:01:18,658 --> 00:01:21,532
gravity keeps pulling that weight down,

40
00:01:21,532 --> 00:01:24,038
so the badge always stays upright.

41
00:01:24,388 --> 00:01:26,142
It works like a pendulum.

42
00:01:26,322 --> 00:01:28,682
The wheel rotates around the badge,

43
00:01:28,682 --> 00:01:31,177
but the weight keeps the badge level,

44
00:01:31,177 --> 00:01:33,604
the same way a hanging picture stays

45
00:01:33,604 --> 00:01:36,301
straight while you turn the frame around

46
00:01:36,301 --> 00:01:36,504
it.

47
00:01:36,684 --> 00:01:40,654
Rolls-Royce calls them self righting wheel centres.

48
00:01:40,834 --> 00:01:43,154
They became a feature of its cars

49
00:01:43,154 --> 00:01:44,631
in the two thousands.

50
00:01:44,980 --> 00:01:45,863
Why bother?

51
00:01:46,043 --> 00:01:49,417
Because photos of parked cars always show

52
00:01:49,417 --> 00:01:51,556
a perfectly straight logo,

53
00:01:51,556 --> 00:01:53,449
and when the car moves,

54
00:01:53,449 --> 00:01:55,424
the logo stays readable.

55
00:01:55,604 --> 00:01:57,168
It is a small detail,

56
00:01:57,168 --> 00:01:59,327
but it says the same thing as

57
00:01:59,327 --> 00:02:00,817
the rest of the car.

58
00:02:00,997 --> 00:02:02,947
Even the wheels should look calm.

59
00:02:03,297 --> 00:02:05,875
Why is there an umbrella hidden inside

60
00:02:05,875 --> 00:02:07,639
the door of a Rolls-Royce?

61
00:02:07,819 --> 00:02:10,117
Because the moment of getting out of

62
00:02:10,117 --> 00:02:12,288
the car is part of the experience.

63
00:02:12,468 --> 00:02:13,329
If it rains,

64
00:02:13,329 --> 00:02:15,981
the passenger should not step out and

65
00:02:15,981 --> 00:02:18,418
get wet while someone looks for an

66
00:02:18,418 --> 00:02:19,063
umbrella.

67
00:02:19,243 --> 00:02:21,157
So it sits in a tube inside

68
00:02:21,157 --> 00:02:23,214
the door, ready to slide out.

69
00:02:23,563 --> 00:02:26,431
The engineering problem is the water.

70
00:02:26,611 --> 00:02:28,919
A wet umbrella put back into a

71
00:02:28,919 --> 00:02:31,380
door would drip into the car and

72
00:02:31,380 --> 00:02:33,380
could damage it over time.

73
00:02:33,560 --> 00:02:35,969
So the umbrella sits in its own

74
00:02:35,969 --> 00:02:38,767
compartment, designed to let it dry,

75
00:02:38,767 --> 00:02:41,176
away from the rest of the door.

76
00:02:41,356 --> 00:02:44,037
The fabric is also treated to shed

77
00:02:44,037 --> 00:02:45,141
water quickly.

78
00:02:45,490 --> 00:02:47,003
It is a tiny part,

79
00:02:47,003 --> 00:02:49,441
but it became one of the most

80
00:02:49,441 --> 00:02:51,795
famous details of the brand.

81
00:02:51,975 --> 00:02:54,808
It shows how Rolls-Royce thinks.

82
00:02:54,988 --> 00:02:57,176
Not only about how the car drives,

83
00:02:57,176 --> 00:02:59,494
but about the full minute before and

84
00:02:59,494 --> 00:03:00,524
after the drive,

85
00:03:00,524 --> 00:03:02,906
including the walk to the front door.

86
00:03:03,255 --> 00:03:05,810
Why does the little silver statue on

87
00:03:05,810 --> 00:03:08,933
a Rolls-Royce bonnet disappear into the car?

88
00:03:09,113 --> 00:03:12,126
The statue is the Spirit of Ecstasy,

89
00:03:12,126 --> 00:03:14,720
and it is a target for thieves.

90
00:03:14,900 --> 00:03:16,731
On modern Rolls-Royce cars,

91
00:03:16,731 --> 00:03:18,832
it sits on a mechanism that can

92
00:03:18,832 --> 00:03:20,798
pull it down into the grille.

93
00:03:20,978 --> 00:03:22,667
When the car is locked,

94
00:03:22,667 --> 00:03:24,870
or if someone tries to pull it

95
00:03:24,870 --> 00:03:26,853
off, it drops out of sight.

96
00:03:27,202 --> 00:03:30,360
The mechanism is also about safety.

97
00:03:30,540 --> 00:03:33,146
A hard metal statue on the front

98
00:03:33,146 --> 00:03:35,751
of a car could hurt a pedestrian

99
00:03:35,751 --> 00:03:36,972
in an accident.

100
00:03:37,152 --> 00:03:39,132
If the car hits something,

101
00:03:39,132 --> 00:03:42,331
the mascot is designed to retract quickly,

102
00:03:42,331 --> 00:03:44,234
so it does not stick out.

103
00:03:44,414 --> 00:03:47,792
A beautiful ornament becomes a safer part

104
00:03:47,792 --> 00:03:48,698
of the car.

105
00:03:49,048 --> 00:03:52,081
The statue itself goes back to nineteen

106
00:03:52,081 --> 00:03:54,726
eleven, sculpted by Charles Sykes.

107
00:03:54,906 --> 00:03:56,835
More than a century later,

108
00:03:56,835 --> 00:03:58,690
it is still on every car,

109
00:03:58,690 --> 00:04:01,435
now made lower and slightly leaner to

110
00:04:01,435 --> 00:04:02,696
help the airflow.

111
00:04:02,876 --> 00:04:04,526
On the electric Spectre,

112
00:04:04,526 --> 00:04:07,414
Rolls-Royce reshaped it to cut through the

113
00:04:07,414 --> 00:04:08,170
air better.

114
00:04:08,520 --> 00:04:10,525
Why do the rear doors of a

115
00:04:10,525 --> 00:04:12,607
Rolls-Royce open backwards?

116
00:04:12,787 --> 00:04:14,820
They are hinged at the rear,

117
00:04:14,820 --> 00:04:16,999
like the doors of an old horse

118
00:04:16,999 --> 00:04:20,121
drawn coach, which is why Rolls-Royce calls

119
00:04:20,121 --> 00:04:21,355
them coach doors.

120
00:04:21,535 --> 00:04:23,118
With the door open,

121
00:04:23,118 --> 00:04:25,700
there is no door frame in front

122
00:04:25,700 --> 00:04:27,117
of the passenger,

123
00:04:27,117 --> 00:04:30,115
so they can step out facing forward,

124
00:04:30,115 --> 00:04:31,532
upright and calm.

125
00:04:31,881 --> 00:04:33,731
With a normal rear door,

126
00:04:33,731 --> 00:04:36,505
you twist your body and squeeze past

127
00:04:36,505 --> 00:04:38,046
the door to get out.

128
00:04:38,226 --> 00:04:39,590
With a coach door,

129
00:04:39,590 --> 00:04:42,394
you simply stand up and walk forward.

130
00:04:42,574 --> 00:04:44,736
And when the front and rear doors

131
00:04:44,736 --> 00:04:45,653
are both open,

132
00:04:45,653 --> 00:04:47,814
the whole side of the cabin opens

133
00:04:47,814 --> 00:04:48,600
like a gate.

134
00:04:48,780 --> 00:04:50,988
It makes getting in and out look

135
00:04:50,988 --> 00:04:53,609
elegant, which matters for a car often

136
00:04:53,609 --> 00:04:54,782
filmed at events.

137
00:04:55,132 --> 00:04:57,902
Rear hinged doors can be dangerous if

138
00:04:57,902 --> 00:05:00,074
they swing open while moving,

139
00:05:00,074 --> 00:05:02,095
which is why they had a bad

140
00:05:02,095 --> 00:05:03,817
reputation in the past.

141
00:05:03,997 --> 00:05:07,980
Modern Rolls-Royce doors are locked while driving,

142
00:05:07,980 --> 00:05:10,848
and a button inside closes them with

143
00:05:10,848 --> 00:05:11,485
a motor.

144
00:05:11,665 --> 00:05:14,591
The passenger never has to stretch out

145
00:05:14,591 --> 00:05:16,669
and pull a heavy door shut.

146
00:05:17,019 --> 00:05:19,005
Why is there a sky full of

147
00:05:19,005 --> 00:05:21,907
stars on the ceiling of a Rolls-Royce?

148
00:05:22,087 --> 00:05:24,572
It is called the Starlight headliner.

149
00:05:24,752 --> 00:05:27,028
Hundreds or even more than a thousand

150
00:05:27,028 --> 00:05:29,365
tiny lights are woven into the leather

151
00:05:29,365 --> 00:05:30,534
of the roof lining.

152
00:05:30,714 --> 00:05:33,044
They are the ends of fibre optic

153
00:05:33,044 --> 00:05:35,957
cables, thin strands of glass that carry

154
00:05:35,957 --> 00:05:37,923
light from a hidden source.

155
00:05:38,273 --> 00:05:40,704
Each point of light is placed by

156
00:05:40,704 --> 00:05:43,439
hand, and customers can even ask for

157
00:05:43,439 --> 00:05:45,034
a real constellation,

158
00:05:45,034 --> 00:05:47,313
like the sky on the night they

159
00:05:47,313 --> 00:05:48,072
were born.

160
00:05:48,252 --> 00:05:51,296
Because the light comes through fibres,

161
00:05:51,296 --> 00:05:53,481
there is no heat and no bulb

162
00:05:53,481 --> 00:05:54,417
in the roof.

163
00:05:54,597 --> 00:05:56,717
The whole sky is lit from a

164
00:05:56,717 --> 00:05:59,543
source far away from the passengers.

165
00:05:59,892 --> 00:06:02,725
The reason is the same calm feeling.

166
00:06:02,905 --> 00:06:06,318
At night, a dark cabin feels small

167
00:06:06,318 --> 00:06:07,422
and closed.

168
00:06:07,602 --> 00:06:10,105
A soft starry sky makes it feel

169
00:06:10,105 --> 00:06:11,478
open and relaxed,

170
00:06:11,478 --> 00:06:14,466
without the glare of a normal reading

171
00:06:14,466 --> 00:06:14,951
light.

172
00:06:15,131 --> 00:06:17,529
It became one of the most requested

173
00:06:17,529 --> 00:06:19,995
options in the history of the brand.

174
00:06:20,345 --> 00:06:23,117
Why does a Rolls-Royce have cameras that

175
00:06:23,117 --> 00:06:24,572
watch the road ahead?

176
00:06:24,752 --> 00:06:26,598
To prepare the suspension.

177
00:06:26,778 --> 00:06:29,738
Rolls-Royce calls the system Flagbearer.

178
00:06:29,918 --> 00:06:32,598
Cameras in the windscreen look at the

179
00:06:32,598 --> 00:06:34,409
road in front of the car,

180
00:06:34,409 --> 00:06:36,075
and if they see a bump,

181
00:06:36,075 --> 00:06:39,407
the suspension adjusts before the wheels reach

182
00:06:39,407 --> 00:06:39,624
it.

183
00:06:39,973 --> 00:06:41,947
The name comes from history.

184
00:06:42,127 --> 00:06:44,307
In the early days of the car

185
00:06:44,307 --> 00:06:46,798
in Britain, a person had to walk

186
00:06:46,798 --> 00:06:49,600
in front of a motor vehicle carrying

187
00:06:49,600 --> 00:06:50,456
a red flag,

188
00:06:50,456 --> 00:06:51,624
to warn others.

189
00:06:51,804 --> 00:06:55,204
Rolls-Royce named its camera after that person,

190
00:06:55,204 --> 00:06:57,880
because it also walks ahead and warns

191
00:06:57,880 --> 00:06:59,978
the car about what is coming.

192
00:07:00,327 --> 00:07:03,384
The goal is what Rolls-Royce calls the

193
00:07:03,384 --> 00:07:04,832
magic carpet ride.

194
00:07:05,012 --> 00:07:08,807
Air springs and electronically controlled dampers soften

195
00:07:08,807 --> 00:07:11,246
each bump, and the camera gives them

196
00:07:11,246 --> 00:07:12,466
time to get ready.

197
00:07:12,646 --> 00:07:14,935
The car should feel like it floats

198
00:07:14,935 --> 00:07:15,878
over the road,

199
00:07:15,878 --> 00:07:17,696
not like it is fighting it.

200
00:07:18,046 --> 00:07:20,434
Why does a Rolls-Royce have no rev

201
00:07:20,434 --> 00:07:20,995
counter?

202
00:07:21,175 --> 00:07:23,860
A normal sports car shows how fast

203
00:07:23,860 --> 00:07:25,675
the engine is spinning,

204
00:07:25,675 --> 00:07:27,886
so the driver can push it to

205
00:07:27,886 --> 00:07:28,675
the limit.

206
00:07:28,855 --> 00:07:32,267
A Rolls-Royce shows a gauge called the

207
00:07:32,267 --> 00:07:34,242
power reserve instead.

208
00:07:34,422 --> 00:07:36,075
It tells you how much of the

209
00:07:36,075 --> 00:07:38,022
engine's power you are not using.

210
00:07:38,371 --> 00:07:41,492
The gauge usually shows a large reserve,

211
00:07:41,492 --> 00:07:44,223
often close to one hundred percent.

212
00:07:44,403 --> 00:07:45,715
That is the point.

213
00:07:45,895 --> 00:07:48,738
The six point seven five litre V

214
00:07:48,738 --> 00:07:52,113
twelve engine is designed to make huge

215
00:07:52,113 --> 00:07:55,134
pulling force at low engine speed,

216
00:07:55,134 --> 00:07:58,509
so the car moves smoothly without ever

217
00:07:58,509 --> 00:07:59,664
working hard.

218
00:07:59,844 --> 00:08:02,629
The gauge reminds the driver how much

219
00:08:02,629 --> 00:08:04,059
is still available.

220
00:08:04,408 --> 00:08:07,012
It is a dashboard that matches the

221
00:08:07,012 --> 00:08:08,008
brand's idea.

222
00:08:08,188 --> 00:08:10,531
A sports car tells you how hard

223
00:08:10,531 --> 00:08:11,589
it is working.

224
00:08:11,769 --> 00:08:15,416
A Rolls-Royce tells you how easy everything

225
00:08:15,416 --> 00:08:15,670
is.

226
00:08:15,850 --> 00:08:18,689
The name sounds like a fine mechanical

227
00:08:18,689 --> 00:08:21,528
watch, where a power reserve shows how

228
00:08:21,528 --> 00:08:23,919
long the watch can keep running.

229
00:08:24,099 --> 00:08:26,084
The idea is the same.

230
00:08:26,264 --> 00:08:27,025
Look at it,

231
00:08:27,025 --> 00:08:29,170
and you know you will never run

232
00:08:29,170 --> 00:08:29,585
short.

233
00:08:29,934 --> 00:08:32,287
Why does the Rolls-Royce grille look like

234
00:08:32,287 --> 00:08:33,893
the front of a Greek temple?

235
00:08:34,073 --> 00:08:36,260
It is called the Pantheon grille,

236
00:08:36,260 --> 00:08:38,578
after the ancient building in Rome.

237
00:08:38,758 --> 00:08:41,060
Its vertical bars and straight,

238
00:08:41,060 --> 00:08:44,921
proud shape were inspired by classical architecture,

239
00:08:44,921 --> 00:08:46,926
and it has been the face of

240
00:08:46,926 --> 00:08:49,079
the brand for over a century.

241
00:08:49,429 --> 00:08:51,659
It started as a working part.

242
00:08:51,839 --> 00:08:54,305
Early cars needed a big radiator at

243
00:08:54,305 --> 00:08:56,984
the front, and the grille protected it

244
00:08:56,984 --> 00:08:58,816
while letting air through.

245
00:08:58,996 --> 00:09:01,528
The vertical bars were simple to make

246
00:09:01,528 --> 00:09:03,512
and let air flow straight in.

247
00:09:03,692 --> 00:09:07,035
Rolls-Royce shaped that functional part to look

248
00:09:07,035 --> 00:09:09,950
dignified, and it never changed the idea.

249
00:09:10,300 --> 00:09:12,206
On the electric Spectre,

250
00:09:12,206 --> 00:09:15,065
there is no engine radiator to cool,

251
00:09:15,065 --> 00:09:16,732
but the grille stays.

252
00:09:16,912 --> 00:09:18,487
On some newer models,

253
00:09:18,487 --> 00:09:20,512
it is even lit from behind.

254
00:09:20,692 --> 00:09:23,498
A part born from cooling became a

255
00:09:23,498 --> 00:09:24,093
symbol.

256
00:09:24,273 --> 00:09:27,596
That is why every Rolls-Royce is recognisable

257
00:09:27,596 --> 00:09:29,590
from a hundred metres away,

258
00:09:29,590 --> 00:09:30,624
even at night.

259
00:09:30,974 --> 00:09:33,038
Why is the thin line along the

260
00:09:33,038 --> 00:09:35,652
side of a Rolls-Royce painted by hand?

261
00:09:35,832 --> 00:09:37,816
It is called the coachline,

262
00:09:37,816 --> 00:09:40,020
and for many years it has been

263
00:09:40,020 --> 00:09:42,886
painted by one craftsman at the factory

264
00:09:42,886 --> 00:09:45,311
in Goodwood, with a brush made of

265
00:09:45,311 --> 00:09:46,339
squirrel hair.

266
00:09:46,519 --> 00:09:47,995
A machine could do it,

267
00:09:47,995 --> 00:09:50,544
but Rolls-Royce wants the line to show

268
00:09:50,544 --> 00:09:51,953
the hand of a person.

269
00:09:52,302 --> 00:09:54,357
The line runs the length of the

270
00:09:54,357 --> 00:09:56,412
car and must be perfectly even.

271
00:09:56,592 --> 00:09:58,596
The painter works freehand,

272
00:09:58,596 --> 00:10:00,896
with a steady hand and years of

273
00:10:00,896 --> 00:10:03,419
practice, and the job takes hours.

274
00:10:03,599 --> 00:10:06,142
Any mistake means starting again.

275
00:10:06,322 --> 00:10:09,378
Customers can ask for their initials or

276
00:10:09,378 --> 00:10:11,964
a small design painted at the end

277
00:10:11,964 --> 00:10:12,905
of the line.

278
00:10:13,255 --> 00:10:15,835
The coachline also goes back to horse

279
00:10:15,835 --> 00:10:18,835
drawn carriages, which had painted lines to

280
00:10:18,835 --> 00:10:21,765
show off the craftsmanship of the builder.

281
00:10:21,945 --> 00:10:24,778
On a Rolls-Royce it is a signature,

282
00:10:24,778 --> 00:10:27,369
a reminder that the car is built

283
00:10:27,369 --> 00:10:28,584
for one person,

284
00:10:28,584 --> 00:10:31,256
not mass produced on a fast line.

285
00:10:31,606 --> 00:10:34,914
Why is a Rolls-Royce so quiet inside?

286
00:10:35,094 --> 00:10:37,912
Because silence is engineered,

287
00:10:37,912 --> 00:10:39,320
piece by piece.

288
00:10:39,500 --> 00:10:43,101
Rolls-Royce uses more than a hundred kilograms

289
00:10:43,101 --> 00:10:45,606
of sound insulation in its cars,

290
00:10:45,606 --> 00:10:46,624
in the floor,

291
00:10:46,624 --> 00:10:49,285
the doors, the roof and around the

292
00:10:49,285 --> 00:10:49,833
engine.

293
00:10:50,013 --> 00:10:52,722
The glass is made with two layers,

294
00:10:52,722 --> 00:10:55,830
with a sound blocking layer in between.

295
00:10:56,180 --> 00:10:58,176
Even the tyres are special.

296
00:10:58,356 --> 00:11:00,720
They have a layer of foam inside,

297
00:11:00,720 --> 00:11:03,371
which absorbs the hollow sound that a

298
00:11:03,371 --> 00:11:05,520
normal tyre makes as it rolls.

299
00:11:05,700 --> 00:11:08,810
The aluminium frame is designed to avoid

300
00:11:08,810 --> 00:11:11,841
vibrations that could hum in the cabin.

301
00:11:12,021 --> 00:11:14,667
Each source of noise has its own

302
00:11:14,667 --> 00:11:15,412
solution.

303
00:11:15,762 --> 00:11:18,586
The engineers even found that a cabin

304
00:11:18,586 --> 00:11:19,883
can be too quiet.

305
00:11:20,063 --> 00:11:21,909
In near total silence,

306
00:11:21,909 --> 00:11:25,012
people start to hear small sounds and

307
00:11:25,012 --> 00:11:26,019
feel uneasy.

308
00:11:26,199 --> 00:11:29,079
So Rolls-Royce tuned the sound of the

309
00:11:29,079 --> 00:11:30,713
cabin to keep a soft,

310
00:11:30,713 --> 00:11:33,281
low background, like a calm room.

311
00:11:33,461 --> 00:11:35,688
Silence, it turns out,

312
00:11:35,688 --> 00:11:38,117
also has to be designed.

313
00:11:38,467 --> 00:11:39,918
So here are the ten.

314
00:11:40,098 --> 00:11:42,977
A floating logo that stays upright.

315
00:11:43,157 --> 00:11:45,084
An umbrella in the door.

316
00:11:45,264 --> 00:11:47,203
A statue that hides.

317
00:11:47,383 --> 00:11:49,589
Doors that open backwards.

318
00:11:49,769 --> 00:11:51,615
Stars on the ceiling.

319
00:11:51,795 --> 00:11:53,838
A camera that reads the road.

320
00:11:54,018 --> 00:11:56,288
A gauge that shows the power you

321
00:11:56,288 --> 00:11:57,281
are not using.

322
00:11:57,461 --> 00:11:59,075
A temple shaped grille.

323
00:11:59,255 --> 00:12:01,159
A line painted by hand.

324
00:12:01,339 --> 00:12:03,863
And a cabin where even the silence

325
00:12:03,863 --> 00:12:04,903
is engineered.

326
00:12:05,253 --> 00:12:06,983
Luxury, at this level,

327
00:12:06,983 --> 00:12:10,129
is really engineering that hides effort.

328
00:12:10,309 --> 00:12:13,375
If you want more machines explained part

329
00:12:13,375 --> 00:12:16,288
by part, subscribe to Machine Reverse.

330
00:12:16,468 --> 00:12:18,867
And tell us in the comments which

331
00:12:18,867 --> 00:12:21,994
detail of a Rolls-Royce surprised you most.
